A||N||11||2xsess||1500 mile trip in my Fiero||||10||
Z||000000||2xsess||12-10-2000||05:53 PM||||Well, I just got back from West Palm Beach, FL. I left early Friday morning. I had the oil changed and 2 new tires put on Thursday. <P>The really sad part of the whole trip was that I only saw 2 Fieros the whole time. The first one wasn't until I was all the way in West Palm Beach. It was a white formula with a female driver, it looked like it was it good condition. I didn't give chase because I was heading the other way in morning rush hour traffic.<BR>The second one has today on the was home, I saw it through the guardrail as it was heading the opposite way. It was a red fastback, I passed it near Jacksonville, any one here own this one?<P>Other than that I saw a bunch of Vettes and a handful of Vipers, too bad they were all going the other way or I could have come back with a Viper kill story  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> (it would go something like this Viper kicked my A$$)lol<P>I was so proud of my car, it ran excellent the entire trip. only the )*%^#$@#^!%$* code 32 all the time. I have to fix that soon.<P>Well, I just wanted to share my story<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Stoic||12-10-2000||06:27 PM||||Thers nothing better than taking a road trip in your fiero.  Exept taking a road trip with a group of fieros.  I always manage to run into somebady along the way.  It's really neat to meet new people with the same interest in the car||||reg||6
Z||000002||WampusCat||12-10-2000||07:05 PM||||I did a 700 mile trip in my new(to me)88 GT this weekend and didn't see another Fiero.  I was nice to find some curvy back roads in Alabama.  None of those around here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I did get sort of a wave from a guy in a firebird until he realized it wasn't another firebird and got a puzzled look on his face.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||12-10-2000||08:24 PM||||Ha! The "near wave".  I've gotten a few of those too.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||wkayl||12-11-2000||12:43 AM||||I have a fix for the "code 32" when you are on vacation....<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/code_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||12-11-2000||12:53 AM||||Jeff, glad you made it back and around safely.  <BR>That pic above is funny, reminds me when I bought my '88 coupe. I couldn't figure out why it wasn't setting any codes, once I looked close enough I notice someone put black electrical tape under the trim, covering the check engine light. The dumb things people do!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||12-11-2000||01:02 AM||||Of ALL the places to go and you go to Palm Beach, Fl?!!! LOL...Didnt run over any dimpled chads did ya?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000007||2xsess||12-11-2000||06:53 AM||||I like the pic of the instant fix  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Fortunetly my "Service engine soon" light isn't very bright so it didn't bother me that much.<P>Thanks Joel<P>It's not like I wanted them to count anything for me. Just visiting family. <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000008||2birds||12-11-2000||11:38 PM||||I was Xmas shopping in Jacksonville all afternoon on the tenth, so it may have been me you saw.  I got passed by a red GT just like mine near Orange Park Mall.  Figure the odds.  ||||reg||1
